From 7a33a706f5505b2752955e3f8032d8555826b979 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:11:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci(js-tests): run-workspace-checks always runs main; OOM
 count is per run [daveey]

Review of the admission change: guarding main() on import.meta.url ===
argv[1] made the CLI exit 0 having run nothing when started through a
symlink (Node resolves the module URL, not argv[1]). The pure admission
functions move to workspace-check-admission.mjs, which the test imports,
and the CLI calls main() unconditionally.

A runner container can serve many jobs, so memory.events oom_kill is
read before and after and the summary reports the difference; the
memory.peak line says it is since cgroup start. Tests: the CLI lists
units through a symlinked path; oom_kill parsing; the real
apps/desktop manifest test asserts the four units killed together do
not fit together instead of pinning the exact heavy set.
